 \section{Conclusions}
-A small neural current predictor with bounded output-layer updates was evaluated within an ESP32-oriented photovoltaic simulation. The completed static Wokwi pair shows reduced current prediction error after ten updates, while recorded energy is slightly lower than with frozen weights. The programmed host comparison likewise provides no energy benefit from the current update rule. These findings support local model adaptation but not improved energy capture. Dynamic paired Wokwi trials remain necessary to complete the controller assessment.
+A neural MPPT algorithm combining bounded output-layer identification, predicted-power search, voltage-reference regulation and INC fallback was evaluated within an ESP32-oriented photovoltaic simulation. The completed static Wokwi pair shows reduced current prediction error after ten updates, while recorded energy is slightly lower than with frozen weights. The programmed host comparison likewise provides no energy benefit from the current update rule. These findings support local model adaptation but not improved energy capture. Dynamic paired Wokwi trials remain necessary to complete the controller assessment.
 
